{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RHr2tAy714bMZK5nTEfZXD","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→-- Create shadow_players table to track non-registered players in tournaments and rankings\n     2→create table if not exists public.shadow_players (\n     3→  id uuid default gen_random_uuid() primary key,\n     4→  name text not null,\n     5→  created_at timestamptz default now() not null,\n     6→  linked_user_id uuid references public.profiles(id) on delete set null\n     7→);\n     8→\n     9→-- Create unique constraint on name (case-insensitive)\n    10→create unique index shadow_players_name_unique_idx on public.shadow_players (lower(name));\n    11→\n    12→-- Create index on linked_user_id for efficient lookups\n    13→create index shadow_players_linked_user_id_idx on public.shadow_players (linked_user_id);\n    14→\n    15→-- Enable Row Level Security\n    16→alter table public.shadow_players enable row level security;\n    17→\n    18→-- RLS policy: public read access\n    19→create policy \"Anyone can read shadow players\"\n    20→  on public.shadow_players for select\n    21→  using (true);\n    22→\n    23→-- RLS policy: admin write operations\n    24→-- Note: service_role bypasses RLS entirely, so these policies apply to authenticated users only\n    25→-- For now, no authenticated users can write - all write operations go through service_role (server-side)\n    26→-- When an admin role system is implemented, update these policies to check admin status\n    27→create policy \"Admin can insert shadow players\"\n    28→  on public.shadow_players for insert\n    29→  with check (false);\n    30→\n    31→create policy \"Admin can update shadow players\"\n    32→  on public.shadow_players for update\n    33→  using (false);\n    34→\n    35→create policy \"Admin can delete shadow players\"\n    36→  on public.shadow_players for delete\n    37→  using (false);\n    38→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xf9UPEbzNoWEcFBNCVrL3V","session_id":"d31604bc-0b46-4e4a-be70-ac7181480a59","uuid":"7b4fbfad-04c4-44ef-93dd-fd44e3250ed1"}
