{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015NYUNUMuTk3HPPnosseNFN","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→import { NextResponse } from \"next/server\";\n     2→import { supabase } from \"@/lib/supabase\";\n     3→\n     4→export async function GET(request: Request) {\n     5→  const { searchParams } = new URL(request.url);\n     6→  const username = searchParams.get(\"username\");\n     7→\n     8→  if (!username) {\n     9→    return NextResponse.json(\n    10→      { error: \"Username parameter is required\" },\n    11→      { status: 400 }\n    12→    );\n    13→  }\n    14→\n    15→  if (username.length < 2) {\n    16→    return NextResponse.json(\n    17→      { error: \"Username must be at least 2 characters\" },\n    18→      { status: 400 }\n    19→    );\n    20→  }\n    21→\n    22→  try {\n    23→    const { data, error } = await supabase\n    24→      .from(\"profiles\")\n    25→      .select(\"full_name\")\n    26→      .ilike(\"full_name\", username)\n    27→      .maybeSingle();\n    28→\n    29→    if (error) {\n    30→      // If table doesn't exist yet, treat username as available\n    31→      if (error.code === \"42P01\") {\n    32→        return NextResponse.json({ available: true });\n    33→      }\n    34→      throw error;\n    35→    }\n    36→\n    37→    return NextResponse.json({ available: !data });\n    38→  } catch (error) {\n    39→    console.error(\"Error checking username:\", error);\n    40→    return NextResponse.json(\n    41→      { error: \"Failed to check username availability\" },\n    42→      { status: 500 }\n    43→    );\n    44→  }\n    45→}\n    46→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xf9UPEbzNoWEcFBNCVrL3V","session_id":"d31604bc-0b46-4e4a-be70-ac7181480a59","uuid":"de86eeba-4943-4e8b-9ebd-7f2640876f19"}
