{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BGRPb12AwWdUMoXTiFpeNx","type":"tool_result","content":"b4d3375 feat: US-017 - User membership application flow\n031a532 feat: US-017 - User membership application flow\n48e9c5b feat: US-016 - Create membership database schema\nb14afe5 feat: US-016 - Create membership database schema\n9b60dfb feat: US-014 - Build educational section public pages\n68ad706 feat: US-014 - Build educational section public pages\n5ba014a feat: US-013 - Create educational content database schema\neb4c4c3 feat: US-013 - Create educational content database schema\n32e6562 feat: US-010 - Create shadow player database schema\nf0c9eb2 feat: US-010 - Create shadow player database schema","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xf9UPEbzNoWEcFBNCVrL3V","session_id":"d31604bc-0b46-4e4a-be70-ac7181480a59","uuid":"80e760dc-721d-450a-b803-3efc650040dc"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xf9UPEbzNoWEcFBNCVrL3V","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information I need. Let me compile a comprehensive summary.\n\n## Codebase Exploration Summary\n\nI've thoroughly explored the roundnet codebase to understand the database structure, migrations, and existing patterns. Here's what I found:\n\n### 1. Migration File Naming Convention\n\n**Format:** `YYYYMMDDHHmmmm_description.sql`\n\n**Existing migrations:**\n- `/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/supabase/migrations/20260202000000_create_profiles_table.sql`\n- `/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/supabase/migrations/20260202100000_create_shadow_players_table.sql`\n- `/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/supabase/migrations/20260202200000_create_educational_content_table.sql`\n- `/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/supabase/migrations/20260202300000_create_memberships_table.sql`\n- `/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/supabase/migrations/20260202310000_create_membership_payments_table.sql`\n\nThe convention uses date with incremental timestamps to order migrations sequentially.\n\n### 2. Existing Tables and Foreign Key Relationships\n\n**profiles table:**\n```sql\n- id (uuid, references auth.users)\n- full_name (text, unique)\n- email (text)\n- created_at, updated_at (timestamptz)\n```\n\n**shadow_players table:**\n```sql\n- id (uuid, primary key)\n- name (text, unique - case insensitive)\n- created_at (timestamptz)\n- linked_user_id (uuid, references profiles(id) on delete set null)\n```\n\n**memberships table (references profiles):**\n```sql\n- id (uuid, primary key)\n- user_id (uuid, references profiles(id) on delete cascade)\n- status (enum: 'pending', 'active', 'expired')\n- applied_at, approved_at, expires_at (timestamptz)\n- payment_reference (text)\n```\n\n**membership_payments table (references memberships):**\n```sql\n- id (uuid, primary key)\n- membership_id (uuid, references memberships(id) on delete cascade)\n- amount (numeric(10, 2))\n- payment_method (enum: 'bizum', 'transfer')\n- status (enum: 'pending', 'verified')\n- verified_at, verified_by (uuid, references profiles(id) on delete set null)\n```\n\n**educational_content table:**\n```sql\n- id (uuid, primary key)\n- title_es, title_en, content_es, content_en (text)\n- category (enum: 'rules', 'formats', 'general_info', 'videos')\n- video_url (text)\n- sort_order (integer)\n- created_at (timestamptz)\n```\n\n### 3. RLS Policy Patterns\n\nThe codebase uses consistent RLS patterns:\n\n**User-owned data pattern (profiles, memberships, membership_payments):**\n```sql\n-- Users can view their own data\ncreate policy \"Users can view own {table}\"\n  on public.{table} for select\n  using (auth.uid() = user_id);\n\n-- Users can update their own data\ncreate policy \"Users can update own {table}\"\n  on public.{table} for update\n  using (auth.uid() = user_id);\n\n-- Users can insert their own data\ncreate policy \"Users can {action} own {table}\"\n  on public.{table} for insert\n  with check (auth.uid() = user_id);\n```\n\n**Admin-controlled data pattern (shadow_players, educational_content):**\n```sql\n-- Public read access\ncreate policy \"Anyone can read {table}\"\n  on public.{table} for select\n  using (true);\n\n-- Admin write operations (currently blocking all authenticated users)\ncreate policy \"Admin can insert {table}\"\n  on public.{table} for insert\n  with check (false);  -- Placeholder: will be updated when admin role exists\n\n-- Note: Service role bypasses RLS entirely for server-side operations\n```\n\n**Nested table access pattern (membership_payments):**\n```sql\n-- Users can view payments related to their own memberships\ncreate policy \"Users can view own membership payments\"\n  on public.membership_payments for select\n  using (\n    exists (\n      select 1 from public.memberships\n      where memberships.id = membership_payments.membership_id\n      and memberships.user_id = auth.uid()\n    )\n  );\n```\n\n### 4. Key Database Patterns and Conventions\n\n**Enums used:**\n- `membership_status` (pending, active, expired)\n- `payment_method` (bizum, transfer)\n- `payment_status` (pending, verified)\n- `educational_content_category` (rules, formats, general_info, videos)\n\n**Indexing patterns:**\n- Foreign key columns indexed (user_id, membership_id, linked_user_id)\n- Status columns indexed for filtering\n- Case-insensitive unique constraints using `lower(column_name)`\n- Sort order columns indexed for efficient ordering\n\n**Timestamps:**\n- `created_at` (defaults to `now()`)\n- `updated_at` (auto-updated via trigger)\n- Approval/verification timestamps for state transitions\n\n**Soft deletes:** Not used. Instead, cascade deletes on foreign keys.\n\n**Trigger patterns:**\n- `handle_new_user()` - creates profile on auth user signup\n- `update_updated_at_column()` - maintains updated_at timestamp\n\n### 5. Tournament-Related Code\n\n**Currently: NO existing tournament or team tables**\n\nHowever, the codebase shows patterns that should be followed:\n- User types in membership-content.tsx define data structures\n- API endpoints use Supabase client directly\n- RLS policies handle user authorization\n- Enums for status fields\n\n**Frontend patterns to follow:**\n- TypeScript types mirror database structure\n- React hooks for data loading\n- Zod validation for forms\n- Supabase client imports from `@/lib/supabase`\n\n### 6. References for tournament_team_members\n\nThe `tournament_team_members` table will need to reference:\n- **profiles table** (for user_id foreign key)\n- **shadow_players table** (for non-registered players)\n- Future **tournaments table** (for tournament_id foreign key)\n- Future **teams table** (for team_id foreign key)\n\n### Recommendations for tournament_team_members Migration\n\nBased on patterns found, the migration should:\n\n1. **Use next timestamp** in sequence (probably `20260202400000_*` or later depending on other tables needed first)\n2. **Include enums** for player role if needed (e.g., 'member', 'substitute')\n3. **Add indexes** on foreign keys and status fields\n4. **Enable RLS** with appropriate policies:\n   - Tournament organizers can read/manage team members\n   - Users can view members of teams they participate in\n5. **Reference both tables**: Support both registered users (via profiles.id) and unregistered players (via shadow_players.id)\n6. **Add timestamps**: created_at, and possibly updated_at\n7. **Include nullable fields** appropriately (e.g., user_id OR shadow_player_id, not both required)"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a1e3176 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d31604bc-0b46-4e4a-be70-ac7181480a59","uuid":"aa69183e-e63c-4952-bb5f-3c2cc6926474","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Explore the codebase to understand:\n1. How database migrations are structured (look for supabase/migrations folder)\n2. Existing table patterns and naming conventions\n3. Any existing shadow_player or user-related tables that tournament_team_members will reference\n4. RLS policy patterns used in other migrations\n\nFocus on finding migration files and understanding the schema structure. Return a summary of:\n- Migration file naming convention\n- Existing tables that tournaments will reference (users, shadow_players, etc.)\n- RLS policy patterns\n- Any existing tournament-related code","agentId":"a1e3176","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information I need. Let me compile a comprehensive summary.\n\n## Codebase Exploration Summary\n\nI've thoroughly explored the roundnet codebase to understand the database structure, migrations, and existing patterns. Here's what I found:\n\n### 1. Migration File Naming Convention\n\n**Format:** `YYYYMMDDHHmmmm_description.sql`\n\n**Existing migrations:**\n- `/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/supabase/migrations/20260202000000_create