rship_payments):**\n```sql\n-- Users can view their own data\ncreate policy \"Users can view own {table}\"\n  on public.{table} for select\n  using (auth.uid() = user_id);\n\n-- Users can update their own data\ncreate policy \"Users can update own {table}\"\n  on public.{table} for update\n  using (auth.uid() = user_id);\n\n-- Users can insert their own data\ncreate policy \"Users can {action} own {table}\"\n  on public.{table} for insert\n  with check (auth.uid() = user_id);\n```\n\n**Admin-controlled data pattern (shadow_players, educational_content):**\n```sql\n-- Public read access\ncreate policy \"Anyone can read {table}\"\n  on public.{table} for select\n  using (true);\n\n-- Admin write operations (currently blocking all authenticated users)\ncreate policy \"Admin can insert {table}\"\n  on public.{table} for insert\n  with check (false);  -- Placeholder: will be updated when admin role exists\n\n-- Note: Service role bypasses RLS entirely for server-side operations\n```\n\n**Nested table access pattern (membership_payments):**\n```sql\n-- Users can view payments related to their own memberships\ncreate policy \"Users can view own membership payments\"\n  on public.membership_payments for select\n  using (\n    exists (\n      select 1 from public.memberships\n      where memberships.id = membership_payments.membership_id\n      and memberships.user_id = auth.uid()\n    )\n  );\n```\n\n### 4. Key Database Patterns and Conventions\n\n**Enums used:**\n- `membership_status` (pending, active, expired)\n- `payment_method` (bizum, transfer)\n- `payment_status` (pending, verified)\n- `educational_content_category` (rules, formats, general_info, videos)\n\n**Indexing patterns:**\n- Foreign key columns indexed (user_id, membership_id, linked_user_id)\n- Status columns indexed for filtering\n- Case-insensitive unique constraints using `lower(column_name)`\n- Sort order columns indexed for efficient ordering\n\n**Timestamps:**\n- `created_at` (defaults to `now()`)\n- `updated_at` (auto-updated via trigger)\n- Approval/verification timestamps for state transitions\n\n**Soft deletes:** Not used. Instead, cascade deletes on foreign keys.\n\n**Trigger patterns:**\n- `handle_new_user()` - creates profile on auth user signup\n- `update_updated_at_column()` - maintains updated_at timestamp\n\n### 5. Tournament-Related Code\n\n**Currently: NO existing tournament or team tables**\n\nHowever, the codebase shows patterns that should be followed:\n- User types in membership-content.tsx define data structures\n- API endpoints use Supabase client directly\n- RLS policies handle user authorization\n- Enums for status fields\n\n**Frontend patterns to follow:**\n- TypeScript types mirror database structure\n- React hooks for data loading\n- Zod validation for forms\n- Supabase client imports from `@/lib/supabase`\n\n### 6. References for tournament_team_members\n\nThe `tournament_team_members` table will need to reference:\n- **profiles table** (for user_id foreign key)\n- **shadow_players table** (for non-registered players)\n- Future **tournaments table** (for tournament_id foreign key)\n- Future **teams table** (for team_id foreign key)\n\n### Recommendations for tournament_team_members Migration\n\nBased on patterns found, the migration should:\n\n1. **Use next timestamp** in sequence (probably `20260202400000_*` or later depending on other tables needed first)\n2. **Include enums** for player role if needed (e.g., 'member', 'substitute')\n3. **Add indexes** on foreign keys and status fields\n4. **Enable RLS** with appropriate policies:\n   - Tournament organizers can read/manage team members\n   - Users can view members of teams they participate in\n5. **Reference both tables**: Support both registered users (via profiles.id) and unregistered players (via shadow_players.id)\n6. **Add timestamps**: created_at, and possibly updated_at\n7. **Include nullable fields** appropriately (e.g., user_id OR shadow_player_id, not both required)"}],"totalD